437	/// Send one request to VFS and return the reply `m_type`.
438	///
439	/// The buffer travels as a **raw address in init's own address space**, not as a
440	/// grant: init is an ordinary user process with no grant table and no privilege to
441	/// issue one. VFS is what turns this address into a magic grant naming init as the
442	/// owner — and it takes that owner from the kernel-stamped `m_source`, never from
443	/// anything in this payload, which is why there is no field here for it.
